          "<b>Why issuers borrow:</b> to finance operations and fill cash shortfalls; to finance expansion and growth plans; and to take advantage of <b>leverage</b> — if a corporation believes it can earn a <b>greater return on cash invested in the business than it would cost to borrow</b>, it increases the return on the business by borrowing.",
